mptcp-bpf-weight-rr (1.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stop forcing net.mptcp.scheduler. The VPS installer installs every
    mptcp-bpf-* package and dh enables and starts each unit, so at boot
    the bpf_dscp, bpf_weight and bpf_weight_rr units each set the sysctl
    to their own scheduler and the last one won: the proxies opened
    their MPTCP listeners with it instead of the scheduler the router
    picked, until a proxy restart. A package upgrade also reset it to
    "default". The unit now only registers the struct_ops; at start it
    applies the scheduler configured in /etc/sysctl.d when that names
    bpf_weight_rr, and at stop it resets the sysctl to "default" only
    when it currently names bpf_weight_rr.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:29:11 +0000

mptcp-bpf-weight-rr (1.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read the subflow stale flag through CO-RE (BPF_CORE_READ_BITFIELD).
    Linux 6.18.55 turned mptcp_subflow_context.stale from a 1-bit field
    into a u8, and the plain subflow->stale was compiled for the bitfield
    of the shipped vmlinux.h: libbpf refused to relocate it and the
    scheduler did not load. The CO-RE read fits both layouts.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:49:06 +0000

